        "content": "<p>alexcrichton opened <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14741\">PR #14741</a> from <code>alexcrichton:fix-panic-when-future-dropped</code> to <code>bytecodealliance:main</code>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>As the test illustrates, it's possible for such a future to be dropped when it has been queued to run (i.e. is no longer in the instance's <code>pending</code> set due to backpressure) but has not yet been run.  Prior to this patch, that led to a panic in <code>TypedFunc::call_async_concurrent::SignalDrop::drop</code>.  This addresses that by modifying <code>StoreOpaque::cancel_guest_subtask_without_lowered_parameters</code> to look for and remove any matching tasks in the<br>\n<code>ConcurrentState::high_priority</code> and <code>ConcurrentState::low_priority</code> queues if they weren't found in the <code>pending</code> set.</p>\n<p>Part of <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/security/advisories/GHSA-3r89-v5mq-j5xf\">https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/security/advisories/GHSA-3r89-v5mq-j5xf</a></p>\n</blockquote>",
